          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            An
            %em abelian group
            (named after
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Niels+Henrik+Abel"} Niels Henrik Abel
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            where the multiplication satisfies the commutative law: for all elements
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x, y\in A
            we have
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mi y
                  %mo =
                  %mi y
                  %mi x
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  x y = y x
                  \\,.
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            with abelian groups as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} objects
            and group homomorphisms as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphisms
            is called
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ab"} Ab
          %p
            Every abelian group has the canonical structure of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module"} module
            over the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+ring"} commutative ring
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi Z
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{Z}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ab"} Ab
            \=
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi Z
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{Z}
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mod"} Mod
          %h3#with_subtraction_and_unit_only With subtraction and unit only
          %p
            This definition of abelian group is based upon
            = succeed "\u2018s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Toby+Bartels"} Toby Bartels
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associative+quasigroup"} associative quasigroup
          %p
            An
            %strong abelian group
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+set"} pointed set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (A, 0)
            with a binary operation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                  %mo ×
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-)-(-):A \times A \to A
            called
            %strong subtraction
            such that
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                for all
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \in A
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                      %mo −
                      %mi a
                      %mo =
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a - a = 0
            %li
              %p
                for all
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \in A
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 0
                      %mo −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 0
                      %mo −
                      %mi a
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mi a
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0 - (0 - a) = a
            %li
              %p
                for all
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \in A
                and
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi b
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b \in A
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                      %mo −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 0
                      %mo −
                      %mi b
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mi b
                      %mo −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 0
                      %mo −
                      %mi a
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a - (0 - b) = b - (0 - a)
            %li
              %p
                for all
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \in A
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi b
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b \in A
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi c
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c \in A
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                      %mo −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi b
                      %mo −
                      %mi c
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi a
                      %mo −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 0
                      %mo −
                      %mi c
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo −
                      %mi b
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a - (b - c) = (a - (0 - c)) - b
          %p
            For every element
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \in A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mi a
                  %mo ≔
                  %mn 0
                  %mo −
                  %mi a
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} -a \coloneqq 0 - a
            and addition is defined as
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo +
                    %mi b
                    %mo ≔
                    %mi a
                    %mo −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a + b \coloneqq a - (-b)
          %p Addition is commutative:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                  %mo +
                  %mi b
                  %mo =
                  %mi a
                  %mo −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 0
                  %mo −
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi b
                  %mo −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 0
                  %mo −
                  %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi b
                  %mo +
                  %mi a
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a + b = a - (0 - b) = b - (0 - a) = b + a
          %p and associative
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo +
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo +
                  %mi c
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 0
                  %mo −
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 0
                  %mo −
                  %mi c
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (a + b) + c = (a - (0 - b)) - (0 - c)
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo +
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo +
                  %mi c
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi b
                  %mo −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 0
                  %mo −
                  %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 0
                  %mo −
                  %mi c
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (a + b) + c = (b - (0 - a)) - (0 - c)
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo +
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo +
                  %mi c
                  %mo =
                  %mi b
                  %mo −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 0
                  %mo −
                  %mi c
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo −
                  %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (a + b) + c = b - ((0 - c) - a)
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo +
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo +
                  %mi c
                  %mo =
                  %mi b
                  %mo −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 0
                  %mo −
                  %mi c
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 0
                  %mo −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 0
                  %mo −
                  %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (a + b) + c = b - ((0 - c) - (0 - (0 - a)))
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo +
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo +
                  %mi c
                  %mo =
                  %mi b
                  %mo −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 0
                  %mo −
                  %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 0
                  %mo −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 0
                  %mo −
                  %mi c
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (a + b) + c = b - ((0 - a) - (0 - (0 - c)))
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo +
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo +
                  %mi c
                  %mo =
                  %mi b
                  %mo −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 0
                  %mo −
                  %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo −
                  %mi c
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (a + b) + c = b - ((0 - a) - c)
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo +
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo +
                  %mi c
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi b
                  %mo −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 0
                  %mo −
                  %mi c
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 0
                  %mo −
                  %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (a + b) + c = (b - (0 - c)) - (0 - a)
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo +
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo +
                  %mi c
                  %mo =
                  %mi a
                  %mo −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 0
                  %mo −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi b
                  %mo −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 0
                  %mo −
                  %mi c
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (a + b) + c = a - (0 - (b - (0 - c)))
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo +
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo +
                  %mi c
                  %mo =
                  %mi a
                  %mo +
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi b
                  %mo +
                  %mi c
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (a + b) + c = a + (b + c)
          %p and has left identities
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 0
                  %mo +
                  %mi a
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                  %mo −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 0
                  %mo −
                  %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi a
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0 + a = 0 - (0 - a) = a
          %p and right identities
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                  %mo +
                  %mn 0
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                  %mo +
                  %mi a
                  %mo =
                  %mi a
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a + 0 = 0 + a = a
          %p and has left inverses
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mi a
                  %mo +
                  %mi a
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 0
                  %mo −
                  %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 0
                  %mo −
                  %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} -a + a = (0 - a) - (0 - a) = 0
          %p and right identities
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                  %mo +
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mi a
                  %mo +
                  %mi a
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a + (-a) = -a + a = 0
          %p Thus, these axioms form an abelian group.
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#in_homotopy_theory In homotopy theory
          %p
            From the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nPOV"} nPOV
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            may be thought of as a (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+object"}> pointed
            )
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid"} groupoid
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G
            with a single object – as discussed at
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delooping"} delooping
            – an abelian group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            may be understood as a (pointed)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-groupoid"} 2-groupoid
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mn 2
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}^2 A
            with a single object and a single morphism: the delooping of the delooping of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mn 2
                  %mi A
                  %mo =
                  %mrow
                    %mo {
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↗
                            %msup
                              %mo ↘
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi Id
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo •
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo ⇓
                              %mrow
                                %mi a
                                %mo ∈
                                %mi A
                          %mtd
                            %mo •
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↘
                            %msub
                              %mo ↗
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi Id
                    %mo }
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathbf{B}^2 A
                  \=
                  \\left\{
                  \\array{
                  \&amp; \nearrow \searrow^{\mathrlap{Id}}
                  \\\
                  \\bullet
                  \&amp;\Downarrow^{a \in A}&amp;
                  \\bullet
                  \\\
                  \&amp; \searrow \nearrow_{\mathrlap{Id}}
                  }
                  \\right\}
                  \\,.
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exchange+law"} exchange law
            for the composition of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-morphisms"} 2-morphisms
            in a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-category"} 2-category
            forces the product on the
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \in A
            here to be commutative. This reasoning is known as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eckmann-Hilton+argument"} Eckmann-Hilton argument
            and is the same as the reasoning that finds that the second
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+group"} homotopy group
            of a space has to be abelian.
          %p
            So the identitfication of abelian groups with one-object, one-morphism 2-groupoids may also be thought of as an identification with 2-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/truncated"} truncated
            and 2-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connected"} connected
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+types"} homotopy types
          %h3#relation_to_other_concepts Relation to other concepts
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoid"} monoid
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ab"} Ab
            with its standard
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal category
            structure, equivalently a (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+object"}> pointed
            )
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ab"} Ab
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category"} enriched category
            with a single object, is a
            = succeed "." do
